```md
# Payroll Automation System

## Project overview

This project automates payroll processing for a part-time and incentive-based workforce.

The business workflow is:

Roster Import → Timesheet Validation → Payroll Calculation → Payroll Approval → Payment Processing

The application is developed as a Nanyang Polytechnic Full Stack Application Development group project.

## Technology stack

### Frontend

- React.js
- Vite
- JavaScript
- Material UI
- React Router DOM
- Axios
- React Hook Form
- Yup

### Backend

- Node.js
- Express.js
- JavaScript
- PostgreSQL
- Sequelize ORM
- JWT authentication
- bcrypt password hashing
- PDFKit
- CSV generation

### Testing

- Jest
- Supertest
- Postman-compatible REST APIs

## Team responsibilities

| Member | Assigned use case |
|---|---|
| Member 1 | UC-001 — Import and synchronise roster working hours |
| Member 2 | UC-002 — Validate and consolidate timesheets |
| Member 3 | UC-003 — Calculate payroll and incentives |
| Member 4 | UC-004 — Review and approve payroll |
| KOK EN QI (XU ENQI) | UC-005 — Generate payment file, synchronise approved payroll to HRMS, and generate payslips |

Authentication, application setup, database configuration, shared routing, and audit infrastructure are shared concerns.

## Member 5 boundary

Member 5 receives only approved and locked payroll periods.

Member 5 does not:

- Recalculate hours
- Recalculate salary
- Recalculate incentives
- Recalculate CPF
- Recalculate SDL
- Change approved gross pay
- Change approved net pay
- Approve or reject payroll

Payment files, HRMS payloads, and payslips use final approved payroll figures from the upstream modules.

